module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.NoetherianRing
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.FlatIsLocal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.RigEtaleArrowIso
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.RigSmoothStability
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Algebra.AdicTopology.CompletionOverNoetherian

/-!
# The annihilation half of rig-étaleness is not a local property

`Rig.RigEtaleCondition` is the annihilation half of rig-étaleness (Stacks 0GCV): for every
witness that an arrow of `WAdm^Noeth` is adic of topologically finite type, the resulting
algebra is rig-étale (Stacks 0GAY). It holds vacuously for an arrow that is not adic of finite
type. This file shows that it is **not** a local property in the sense of Situation 0CBA
(Remark 0ANI), so the hypothesis `hcond` of `Rig.rigEtale_isLocalNoetherian` — and of every
statement that passes it on, among them
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isRigEtale_of_comp`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isRigEtale_pullback_snd_of_isAdicMorphism`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isRigEtale_diagonal_of_isRigEtale`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isFormalModification_pullback_snd` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isRigEtale_of_comp_of_isAdicMorphism_of_mono` — can never be
supplied. The locality of rig-étaleness itself, Stacks 0AQL, is
`Rig.rigEtale_propertyIsLocalNoetherian`, and needs no such input.

## The counterexample

Let `B = ℚ⟦X⟧` (with `X`-adic topology), `T = ℚ⟦X⟧⟨t⟩` its restricted power series ring, and
`A = T × T` with the map `B → A` given by the inclusion on the first factor and by
`ℚ⟦X⟧ → ℚ → T` on the second. The ideal `XA = XT × 0` does not define the product topology,
since the second factor is not discrete, so `B → A` is not adic and the condition holds for it
vacuously. Localizing at the idempotent `(1, 0)` gives the localization diagram with
`A' = T`, `B' = B`, whose completed map is `ℚ⟦X⟧ → ℚ⟦X⟧⟨t⟩` up to isomorphism; that map is adic
of finite type, and it is not rig-étale because its module of differentials is free of rank
one and no power of `X` vanishes in `T`.

## Main results

* `Rig.RigEtaleConditionCounterexample.not_isRigEtaleArrow`: `ℚ⟦X⟧ → ℚ⟦X⟧⟨t⟩` is not
  rig-étale.
* `Rig.RigEtaleConditionCounterexample.not_finiteTypeAdicAlgebraForEveryIdeal`: `B → A` is not
  adic of finite type.
* `Rig.not_propertyIsLocalNoetherian_rigEtaleCondition`: `Rig.RigEtaleCondition` is not a local
  property of arrows of `WAdm^Noeth`, in any universe.

## Implementation notes

`ℚ⟦X⟧` is realised as the `X`-adic completion of `ℚ[X]` and `ℚ⟦X⟧⟨t⟩` as the `X`-adic completion
of the polynomial ring in one variable over it, each with its adic topology. The completions
over `B` of `B` and of `A'` (Stacks 0AN6) are identified with `B` and `A'` themselves through
the comparison with adic completions of `TopologicalRing.CompletionOver.adicCompletionRingEquiv`,
and rig-étaleness transports along these homeomorphisms by
`Rig.isRigEtaleArrow_of_isRigEtaleArrow_of_ringEquiv`.
Non-rig-étaleness of `ℚ⟦X⟧ → ℚ⟦X⟧⟨t⟩` is read off the criterion
`Rig.isRigEtale_adicCompletionObj_iff` (Stacks 0GAF with Stacks 0AJU), the completion being of
the polynomial algebra, whose module of differentials has a basis.

